  "details": "VRCSDK multi-editing issue.\nIf you select two objects that have a VRC_Trigger on them, the trigger type(OnEnterTrigger, etc) of both will be changed to be the same thing, even if you don't change anything.\nIt seems to set it to the value of the one that was created later.\n\nThe same issue also seems to effect the Targets drop down box when using a SendRPC.\n\nnormally in unity differences in drop down boxes when multi editing show as \"--\" for this they don't.\n\nThis is quite frustrating if you don't notice yourself doing it, and especially if you don't know the cause, you might think it just changed for no reason. (and it did, really) It took me about two weeks of solid mapping before i found the cause.\n\nThis post mentions the same issue, https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/multi-object-editing-supports-of-vrctrigger-is-broken",
